{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"display-modes","type":"text","text":"Display Modes\n- displayTimeMode(): Shows current time\n- displayDateMode(): Shows current date\n- displayTemperatureMode(): Shows temperature\n- displayHumidityMode(): Shows humidity\n- displayScrollMode(): Scrolls custom text\n- displayCountdownMode(): Shows countdown timer\n- displayStopwatchMode(): Shows elapsed time\n- displayScoreboardMode(): Shows custom scores\n- displayLightshowMode(): Shows visual effects\n- displayRealtimeMode(): Shows audio visualization","x":-800,"y":-500,"width":350,"height":230},
		{"id":"memory-management","type":"text","text":"Memory Management\n- memoryMonitor: Tracks heap usage\n- logMemoryStatus(): Records memory metrics\n- Memory optimization techniques:\n  - Static buffer allocation\n  - Circular indexing for text scrolling\n  - Careful string handling\n  - Buffer reuse for LED patterns\n  - Heap fragmentation monitoring","x":-800,"y":-230,"width":350,"height":180},
		{"id":"time-management","type":"text","text":"Time Management\n- printLocalTime(): Gets and formats time\n- checkSleepTimer(): Manages sleep schedule\n- BlinkDots(): Handles time separator\n- RTC module integration\n- NTP synchronization\n- Time-based event triggers\n- Countdown and stopwatch functions","x":-800,"y":40,"width":350,"height":180},
		{"id":"main-loop-flow","type":"text","text":"Main Loop Flow\n1. Handle web requests\n2. Check WiFi connection\n3. Process time-based events\n4. Check schedules\n5. Read sensors\n6. Update display mode\n7. Process audio (if enabled)\n8. Monitor memory usage\n9. Handle sleep/wake states","x":-800,"y":260,"width":350,"height":200},
		{"id":"future-improvements","type":"text","text":"Future Improvements\n- Further memory optimization\n- Enhanced error handling\n- Code modularization\n- Improved documentation\n- Performance benchmarking\n- Unit test implementation\n- More visualization modes\n- Enhanced web interface","x":-800,"y":500,"width":350,"height":180},
		{"id":"web-request-flow","type":"text","text":"Web Request Flow\n1. Client connects to server\n2. Server routes request to handler\n3. Handler processes request\n4. Settings updated if needed\n5. Display mode changed if requested\n6. Response sent to client\n7. Memory impact monitored\n8. Changes saved to flash if required","x":900,"y":-1140,"width":350,"height":325},
		{"id":"optimization-notes","type":"text","text":"Optimization Notes\n- LED updates batched for efficiency\n- Web handlers use async where possible\n- Sensor readings filtered to reduce noise\n- Time-based events use millis() for accuracy\n- Display modes optimize LED updates\n- Memory monitoring has minimal overhead\n- String operations minimized in core loops\n- Static buffers preferred over dynamic","x":1305,"y":-1140,"width":525,"height":325},
		{"id":"settings-management","type":"text","text":"Settings Management\n- getclockSettings(): Loads settings from JSON\n- saveclockSettings(): Saves settings to flash\n- processSchedules(): Handles scheduled events\n- createSchedulesArray(): Parses schedule data\n- Configuration for:\n  - Colors\n  - Display modes\n  - Timers and alarms\n  - Visual effects\n  - Network settings","x":160,"y":-1220,"width":500,"height":360},
		{"id":"critical-functions","type":"text","text":"Critical Functions\n- setup(): System initialization\n- loop(): Main program cycle\n- displayTimeMode(): Primary display function\n- loadWebPageHandlers(): Web API setup\n- getclockSettings(): Configuration loading\n- saveclockSettings(): Configuration saving\n- processSchedules(): Event scheduling\n- readAndProcessAudio(): Sound processing","x":310,"y":-47,"width":350,"height":455},
		{"id":"code-structure","type":"text","text":"Code Structure\n- Global variables and configuration\n- Hardware-specific definitions\n- Setup and initialization\n- Main program loop\n- Display mode functions\n- Visual effect functions\n- Audio processing functions\n- File and settings management\n- Web interface handlers\n- Helper utilities","x":310,"y":-472,"width":350,"height":355},
		{"id":"function-interactions","type":"text","text":"Function Interactions\n- setup() → loadWebPageHandlers() → server.on()\n- loop() → displayTimeMode() → displayNumber()\n- readAndProcessAudio() → SpectrumAnalyzer() → FastLED\n- getclockSettings() ↔ saveclockSettings()\n- processSchedules() → various display modes\n- loop() → checkSleepTimer() → brightness control\n- Web handlers → settings → display updates","x":-265,"y":-500,"width":350,"height":450},
		{"id":"visual-effects","type":"text","text":"Visual Effects\n- Twinkles(): Random twinkling lights\n- Rainbow(): Color cycling pattern\n- GreenMatrix(): Matrix-style falling code\n- blueRain(): Rain simulation effect\n- Fire2021(): Fire simulation effect\n- Snake(): Snake game visualization\n- Cylon(): Scanning light pattern\n- Chase(): Chasing light sequence","x":-265,"y":-25,"width":350,"height":335},
		{"id":"memory-optimization","type":"text","text":"Memory Optimization Techniques\n- Static allocation for LED arrays\n- Reuse of color buffers\n- Careful string handling in scroll()\n- Optimized JSON parsing\n- Memory-efficient text scrolling\n- Heap fragmentation prevention\n- Buffer sharing between display modes\n- Minimized dynamic allocations","x":-800,"y":730,"width":350,"height":320},
		{"id":"memory-monitor","type":"text","text":"Memory Monitor System\n- Tracks heap usage and fragmentation\n- Provides historical memory data\n- Web dashboard visualization\n- Alert thresholds for low memory\n- Identifies memory leaks\n- Monitors allocation patterns\n- Helps prevent crashes\n- Accessible via /memory endpoint","x":-800,"y":1095,"width":350,"height":360},
		{"id":"audio-processing","type":"text","text":"Audio Processing\n- readAndProcessAudio(): Captures audio data\n- SpectrumAnalyzer(): Performs FFT analysis\n- i2sWaveformRead(): Reads from I2S microphone\n- Visualization modes:\n  - rainbowBars(): Rainbow colored bars\n  - purpleBars(): Purple gradient bars\n  - fireBars(): Fire effect bars\n  - centerBars(): Center-out visualization\n  - waterfall(): Falling spectrum display","x":-265,"y":330,"width":350,"height":500},
		{"id":"sensor-integration","type":"text","text":"Sensor Integration\n- DHT11: Temperature and humidity\n  - Read in displayTemperatureMode()\n  - Read in displayHumidityMode()\n- INMP441: I2S microphone\n  - Used in audio processing\n  - Feeds spectrum analyzer\n- LDR: Light sensor\n  - Controls automatic brightness\n  - GetBrightnessLevel() function","x":-265,"y":865,"width":350,"height":370},
		{"id":"display-update-flow","type":"text","text":"Display Update Flow\n1. Current mode determines function\n2. Function reads necessary data\n3. LED buffer updated with pattern\n4. Colors applied based on settings\n5. Brightness adjusted (auto/manual)\n6. Special effects applied if enabled\n7. FastLED.show() updates physical LEDs\n8. Memory usage tracked during update","x":-265,"y":1275,"width":350,"height":350},
		{"id":"file-system","type":"text","text":"File System\n- writeFile(): Writes data to LittleFS\n- listDir(): Lists directory contents\n- deleteFile(): Removes files\n- Stores:\n  - Configuration files\n  - Schedule data\n  - Web interface assets\n  - RTTTL song files","x":160,"y":-852,"width":500,"height":315},
		{"id":"setup-function","type":"text","text":"setup()\n- Initializes hardware components\n- Sets up LED display\n- Mounts filesystem\n- Loads settings from JSON\n- Initializes sensors (DHT11, INMP441)\n- Configures WiFi and web server\n- Sets up memory monitoring\n- Initializes RTC module\n- Creates task for parallel processing","x":-1660,"y":-725,"width":360,"height":335},
		{"id":"loop-function","type":"text","text":"loop()\n- Main program cycle\n- Handles web server requests\n- Manages WiFi connection\n- Processes time-based events\n- Runs scheduled tasks\n- Updates display based on mode\n- Monitors memory usage\n- Processes sensor data\n- Manages sleep/wake states","x":-1660,"y":-350,"width":360,"height":385},
		{"id":"initialization-flow","type":"text","text":"Initialization Flow\n1. Hardware setup\n2. LED configuration\n3. File system mounting\n4. Settings loading\n5. Sensor initialization\n6. WiFi connection\n7. Web server setup\n8. Memory monitoring start\n9. Display initial mode","x":-1660,"y":410,"width":360,"height":200},
		{"id":"led-control","type":"text","text":"LED Control\n- FastLED library integration\n- displayNumber(): Shows digits on display\n- allBlank(): Clears all LEDs\n- scroll(): Scrolls text across display\n- colorWheel(): Generates color patterns\n- ShelfDownLights(): Controls accent lighting\n- 273 WS2812B LEDs in 7-segment layout","x":-1680,"y":70,"width":400,"height":280},
		{"id":"core-title","type":"text","text":"ShelfClock Core System","x":-1630,"y":-845,"width":300,"height":60},
		{"id":"web-interface","type":"text","text":"Web Interface\n- loadWebPageHandlers(): Sets up API endpoints\n- server.on(): Defines REST API routes\n- HTTP handlers for:\n  - Settings management\n  - Display control\n  - Scheduler configuration\n  - Memory monitoring\n  - OTA updates\n  - File management","x":-625,"y":-1039,"width":480,"height":345},
		{"id":"error-handling","type":"text","text":"Error Handling\n- WiFi connection retry logic\n- File system mount verification\n- Sensor reading validation\n- Web request validation\n- JSON parsing error checks\n- Memory allocation checks\n- Graceful degradation of features\n- System restart on critical errors","x":235,"y":1275,"width":350,"height":350}
	],
